metrology systems; semiconductor software solutions; KLA Pro systems; and specialty semiconductor manufacturing, benchtop metrology, surface characterization, material strength characterization, and electrical property measurement products. It also provides etch, plasma dicing, deposition and other wafer processing technologies and solutions; direct imaging, inspection, optical shaping, inkjet, and additive printing, as well as computer-aided manufacturing and engineering solutions; and components. In addition, the company offers service programs. It serves semiconductor, and semiconductor-related and electronic device manufacturers. The company operates in China, Taiwan, Korea, North America, Japan, Europe, Israel, and rest of Asia. The company was formerly known as KLA-Tencor Corporation and changed its name to KLA Corporation in July 2019. KLA Corporation was incorporated in 1975 and is headquartered in Milpitas, California.","employees":17000,"website":"https://www.kla.com","country":"United States","city":"Milpitas","officers":[{"name":"Mr. Richard P. Wallace","title":"President, CEO & Executive Director"},{"name":"Mr. Bren D. Higgins","title":"Executive VP & CFO"},{"name":"Ms. Mary Beth Wilkinson","title":"Executive VP, Chief Legal Officer & Corporate Secretary"}]},"sector_medians":{"fpe":17.12,"tpe":29.56,"ps":4.327,"pfcf":26.23,"peg":1.085,"pb":4.643,"ev_ebitda":19.01,"rev_growth":0.1845,"eps_growth":0.356,"eps_growth_fwd":0.2432,"eps_growth_next":0.1828,"div_yield":0,"roe":0.1249,"roa":0.04908,"de":32.04,"gross_margin":0.5312,"op_margin":0.1351,"profit_margin":0.09355,"current_ratio":1.879},"valuation":[{"k":"fpe","label":"Forward P/E","v":21.14,"sector":17.12,"verdict":"Fairly valued"},{"k":"tpe","label":"TTM P/E","v":37.61,"sector":29.56,"verdict":"Overvalued"},{"k":"ps","label":"Price / Sales","v":13.51,"sector":4.327,"verdict":"Overvalued"},{"k":"pfcf","label":"Price / FCF","v":69.56,"sector":26.23,"verdict":"Overvalued"},{"k":"peg","label":"PEG","v":1.